// A primitive arithmetic operator needs its Add/Sub/... witness, which lives in
// @Std/Core. A program that never loads Core has no witness, so `x + x` is a loud
// error (spec/12: operators are trait sugar — primitives are not special-cased,
// so there is no built-in fast path to fall back to). Acceptance soundness.
fn main() {
    val x: I32 = 5
    val y: I32 = x + x
}
